{# /admin/tools: what the derived index holds, and the button that reads every
   file back into it without stopping the site (TASK-95).

   The counts are the point of the screen as much as the button is: an index
   that disagrees with the files is not something the site complains about, so
   the only way to notice is to be shown what it holds. #}
{% extends "layouts/shell.njk" %}

{% block title %}{{ heading }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <h1>{{ heading }}</h1>

  <p>
    Everything in <code>data/geekity.db</code> is a reading of the files under
    <code>{{ contentDir }}</code>, so it can always be read again. Rebuild it after
    editing content outside the admin &mdash; over ssh, or with a
    <code>git pull</code> while the site was down &mdash; or when what is listed here
    disagrees with what is on disk.
  </p>

  <table class="admin-list">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">What the index holds</th>
        <th scope="col">Count</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Documents</th>
        <td>{{ indexed.documents }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Followers</th>
        <td>{{ indexed.followers }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Inbox activities</th>
        <td>{{ indexed.activities }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Comments</th>
        <td>{{ indexed.comments }}</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  {% if confirm %}
    {# Offered rather than done, the way a merge is on the taxonomy screens.
       The window in the middle is the whole reason: for as long as the scan
       runs the site answers 404 for documents whose files are perfectly fine,
       and that is not a thing to discover afterwards. #}
    <form class="admin-settings" method="post" action="{{ rebuildUrl }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
      <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.confirm }}" value="1" />

      <h2>Rebuild the index now?</h2>

      <p>
        The index is emptied and every file read again. Until the scan finishes, this
        site answers <strong>404</strong> for its posts and pages &mdash; under a second
        on a small site, longer on a large one &mdash; and it is serving the whole time.
        Nothing is deleted and nothing is sent: you stay signed in, the delivery log and
        the relays are kept, and no follower, feed or linked page is told about a post
        the scan re-indexes.
      </p>

      <p class="admin-settings-buttons">
        <button type="submit">Rebuild it</button>
        <a href="{{ toolsUrl }}">Cancel</a>
      </p>
    </form>
  {% else %}
    <form class="admin-settings" method="post" action="{{ rebuildUrl }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
      <p class="admin-settings-buttons">
        <button type="submit">Rebuild the index</button>
      </p>
    </form>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="admin-hint">
    This runs on the site as it is: nothing is deleted, no connection is swapped and
    nobody is signed out. <code>geekity rebuild</code> at the command line is the other
    door, and it is for the one case this screen cannot be: a database this version
    refuses to open, where there is no site running to press a button in.
  </p>
{% endblock %}
